{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013UHwEdJWQaXzZUoDggghga","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Native decomposition and review\n2\t\n3\tUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\n4\tand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\n5\tEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\n6\tstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\n7\tSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n8\t\n9\tA blocked proposal is a valid planning outcome. Preserve `OPEN` objections and\n10\t`system_map.unknowns` when ownership, evidence, or product decisions are missing.\n11\tKeep the authored proposal and report the smallest unresolved decision; do not\n12\tclear unknowns or mark objections `ACCEPTED` or `FIXED` merely to make preparation\n13\tpass. Preserve references to applicable unresolved decisions as well; deleting\n14\t`decision_ids` does not resolve the decisions they name. Record resolution or\n15\taccepted risk only from an explicit applicable decision.\n16\tThe reviewer's identity authenticates review; it does not assign seam or swimlane\n17\townership. Record actual owners in the recipe and prepare the corrected topology\n18\tbefore requesting review.\n19\t\n20\tRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\n21\tbefore recording explicit human review:\n22\t\n23\t```bash\n24\ttaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\n25\ttaskspec decompose compile <id>\n26\ttaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n27\ttaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\tReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\n31\tplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\n32\tThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\n33\tand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n34\t\n35\tBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\n36\tcompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\n37\tchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\n38\tdependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\n39\tsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n40\t\n41\tRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n42\t`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n43\t`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\n44\tAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n45\t\n46\tOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n47\t`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\n48\tor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\n49\tapplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"daa3f3ba-460c-4211-ade0-ebf68afc8b7c","uuid":"857a971b-f6a7-4813-9793-11e6785f22c3","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:28:07.231Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat pywtccg8/.agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md","content":"# Native decomposition and review\n\nUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\nand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\nEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\nstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\nSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n\nA blocked proposal is a valid planning outcome. Preserve `OPEN` objections and\n`system_map.unknowns` when ownership, evidence, or product decisions are missing.\nKeep the authored proposal and report the smallest unresolved decision; do not\nclear unknowns or mark objections `ACCEPTED` or `FIXED` merely to make preparation\npass. Preserve references to applicable unresolved decisions as well; deleting\n`decision_ids` does not resolve the decisions they name. Record resolution or\naccepted risk only from an explicit applicable decision.\nThe reviewer's identity authenticates review; it does not assign seam or swimlane\nownership. Record actual owners in the recipe and prepare the corrected topology\nbefore requesting review.\n\nRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\nbefore recording explicit human review:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\ntaskspec decompose compile <id>\ntaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n```\n\nReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\nplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\nThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\nand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n\nBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\ncompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\nchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\ndependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\nsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n\nRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\nAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n\nOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\nor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\napplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf6L3aSpMWfVy8ink7VBF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013JiDT1ERZhuAzanZfurFJm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat pywtccg8\" && find . -name \"*recipe*\" -not -path \"./.git/*\" -not -path \"*/skills/*\" ; echo \"--- skill recipes ---\"; find .agents/skills/task-spec -name \"*rate-limit*\"; echo \"--- status ---\"; taskspec status 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Search for existing recipe files and check status"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1015,"cache_read_input_tokens":14442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1015},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"daa3f3ba-460c-4211-ade0-ebf68afc8b7c","uuid":"6d219d9b-6255-4c63-91fc-5424e3ac776c","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:28:09.138Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6L3ZwJc8RWGxb4DKJB1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013JiDT1ERZhuAzanZfurFJm":{"command":"cd \"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat pywtccg8\" && find . -name \"*recipe*\" -not -path \"./.git/*\" -not -path \"*/skills/*\" ; echo \"--- skill recipes ---\"; find .agents/skills/task-spec -name \"*rate-limit*\"; echo \"--- status ---\"; taskspec status 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Search for existing recipe files and check status"}}}
